---
source: crates/assertrust/tests/cli.rs
expression: run.stdout
---
Check a change for weakened tests

Usage: assertrust check [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --range <RANGE>
          BASE..HEAD checks each commit; BASE...HEAD checks it like a PR (what HEAD adds since it split off from BASE)

      --pr <NUMBER>
          Check a GitHub pull request (merge-base to head)

      --staged
          Check staged changes (HEAD to the git index), for pre-commit hooks

      --worktree
          Check uncommitted changes (HEAD to files on disk), for coding-agent hooks

      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - terminal: Short, human-readable findings
          - json:     Machine-readable findings, for scripts and other tools
          - github:   GitHub Actions annotations
          
          [default: terminal]

      --show-transient
          Also show weakening that was undone later in the same PR

      --fail-on <LEVEL>
          Exit with 1 when a finding is at least this sure (default: never, or `fail-on` in assertrust.toml)

          Possible values:
          - never:  Never fail: findings only warn
          - high:   Fail on high-confidence findings
          - medium: Fail on high- and medium-confidence findings
          - low:    Fail on any finding

  -v, --verbose
          Show the test name, before/after snippets, the full commit message, and changed outcomes

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')
